{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nUnit-test support and cases under `tests/unit/`, excluding the reconciler subtree contain confirmed comment or docstring bloat from the audit pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`. File-specific constraints must survive consolidation.\n\n## Approach\nDelegate remediation to path-disjoint leaf cohorts. Each leaf edits only its recorded file impact, preserves its Scope, and remains independently reviewable. Comments may be reworded or combined; literal-string retention is not required.\n\n## Scope\n- Direct container edits: none; repository edits belong to leaves.\n- Delegated area: Unit-test support and cases under `tests/unit/`, excluding the reconciler subtree.\n- Audited boundary: paths from retired tickets reached through each leaf's net-active `supersedes` links.\n\n## Migration inventory\nAt story completion, read `rebar list --parent popular-stretchy-mussel --full --output json`, follow each net-active supersedes target, and compare source file impacts with replacement Scope and file impact. Store a sorted TSV in a story-linked `session_log`: `path<TAB>replacement-leaf-alias<TAB>source-ticket-alias<TAB>scope-count<TAB>file-impact-count`.\n\nPassing requires one row per audited path, one replacement per source ticket, both counts equal to 1, no extra replacement paths, and equal expected/Scope/file-impact path sets. Record row count and SHA-256 in the completion comment.\n\n## Semantic preservation oracle\nBefore a leaf closes, a reviewer who did not author its remediation compares the base, final patchset, Scope, and file impact. The reviewer stores a leaf-linked TSV: `path<TAB>kind<TAB>scope-item<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>verdict<TAB>reviewer-session`, where kind is `constraint`, `consumer`, or `bloat-removal`.\n\nEvery constraint and consumer contract needs a PASS row with concrete citations. Every edited comment block needs a bloat-removal PASS confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, or historical prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained. Exact substring equality is not the oracle; missing or FAIL rows block closure.\n\nEvery leaf records artifact-specific checks plus an artifact-appropriate prose-only guard. Non-Python paths use a line-oriented comment/blank-line guard. Python paths compare ASTs after stripping docstrings, while focused tests preserve observable `__doc__` and CLI-help contracts. All leaves run path-scoped `git diff --check` and worktree-venv lint. The story log records commands, commits, exit status, and reviewer-log ids.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every audited path has exactly one inventory row with `scope-count=1` and `file-impact-count=1`.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has an independent-review PASS row with before/after citations.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has a bloat-removal PASS row.\n- [ ] Every recorded leaf verification command exits 0 at its cited commit.\n- [ ] The story log records the inventory receipt, command results, and reviewer-log ids.\n\n## Child decomposition\nEach leaf owns its exact path set; leaf sets are disjoint and their union is the audited boundary."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788604592071351424,"uuid":"60a17ea0-0656-41a2-9ead-66b4ce367bf2"}